# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# Build, test and deploy output.
#
# The four rules above only catch the package managers' own crash logs, which is
# not what actually accumulates here: `npm run build > build.log` and
# `bun test > test.log` are how this project is checked, and build.log, build2.log
# and test.log were all sitting untracked in this directory when this rule was
# written. Broad on purpose — nothing in this app's source is a .log.
*.log

# Tarballs. Deploying to the VPS packs changed files with tar before scp'ing
# them, and a stray one left behind is 20 KB of duplicated source.
*.tgz

# env files
#
# Ignored because the values differ per environment and the file is not the same
# on every machine: API_INTERNAL_URL is localhost when everything runs on one
# box, and a private or tunnel address when the backend lives elsewhere.
#
# But the build genuinely DEPENDS on these, and silently: NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL is
# inlined into the client bundle at build time, so if it is missing the viewer
# iframe on /warcs/view points every visitor at their own localhost:3000 and the
# page looks broken for reasons nothing logs. A fresh clone has no way to learn
# that from an ignored file, so .env.example is committed and re-included below.
.env*
!.env.example

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# Editor and OS droppings. Neither belongs to anyone but the machine that made it.
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DELIBERATELY NOT IGNORED — each of these looks ignorable and is load-bearing.
#
#   bun.lock             The real lockfile (160 KB). Note there is also a
#                        92-byte pnpm-lock.yaml stub in this directory that is
#                        vestigial; two lockfiles for two package managers is a
#                        trap, and the pnpm one should be deleted rather than
#                        ignored.
#
#   lib/snapshots/*.json Seed data, not build output. lib/snapshot.ts imports
#                        these statically so the homepage can render real
#                        numbers during a backend outage instead of an empty
#                        panel. A `snapshots/` or `*.json` rule would delete
#                        that safety net without anything failing at build time.
#
#   AGENTS.md            Rewritten by `next dev` on every run. Committing it
#                        with your work keeps the tree clean; ignoring it just
#                        means the next person re-discovers the same warning.
#
#   proxy.ts             Next 16's renamed middleware, and the only thing
#                        redirecting old /warcs/search?q= links into the path.
#                        It is source, despite sitting at the root next to
#                        config files.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
